# Art docs workflow

Full process: `docs/art/WORKFLOW.md`.

- Before starting an art/asset task, name the exact `docs/art/**` files needed and read only those. Do not rely on prior chat history.
- Every completed deliverable is written to `docs/art/<unit>/<unit>-<topic>.md`, standalone, with the header `**Status:** … · **Depends on:** … · **Used by:** …`.
- When a doc changes, update `docs/art/<unit>/README.md` (locked decisions, open items).
- Split large tasks: one sub-task → one doc. Keep chat replies short; the doc is the output.
- After docs change, delegate commit + push to the `github-sync` subagent.
- Scope: one asset at a time. Confirm scope before starting another unit or environment pieces.
